LICENSE DECISION REQUIRED — DO NOT SHIP THIS FILE AS-IS
=========================================================

This file is a placeholder. No license has been chosen for this repository.

Why this is a placeholder and not a license
--------------------------------------------

Skylotus Unity Core is described (see README.md) as the base template Skylotus Studios
clones into every new commercial project. Choosing a license for that — MIT, proprietary,
"all rights reserved", a dual-license split between the studio's own code and the
third-party assets and packages vendored into this repository — is a legal and business
decision about how the studio's commercial IP is allowed to be used, by whom, and under
what terms. That decision belongs to whoever owns the studio's IP strategy, not to an
automated agent filling in a missing file. Guessing wrong here (e.g. silently applying
MIT, which would let anyone reuse Skylotus Studios' core systems freely, including
competitors) is a mistake that is expensive to unwind once the repository has been forked
into real projects and possibly published.

What needs to happen before this file is real
------------------------------------------------

A human with authority over Skylotus Studios' IP needs to decide, at minimum:

1. Is this repository ever intended to be public, or is it strictly an internal template
   cloned into private project repositories (per the README's "delete the .git folder"
   workflow)? That materially changes what "license" even means here — an internal
   template arguably doesn't need an OSS license at all, just an internal usage policy.
2. If it stays internal-only: replace this file with a short proprietary /
   "All Rights Reserved, Skylotus Studios" notice, or remove the file and state the policy
   in the studio's internal documentation instead.
3. If any part of it is ever open-sourced or shared externally: pick an actual license
   (MIT, Apache-2.0, a custom EULA, etc.) with legal input, and confirm every vendored
   third-party asset and package under Assets/ and Packages/ is compatible with that
   choice — this repo bundles third-party packages (LitMotion, TextMeshPro assets, the
   "Animated Loading Icons" asset pack, the UnityEditorDarkMode plugin — see CORE_FIXES.md
   WP-19) each with their own license terms that a top-level LICENSE file does not
   override.
4. Either way, record the decision in README.md so it isn't lost the next time this
   template is forked.

Until that decision is made, treat this repository as "all rights reserved, no license
granted" by default — that is the legal default in the absence of an explicit license, so
this placeholder does not change anyone's rights either way. It exists only as a visible
marker that the decision has not been made yet, rather than silently having no LICENSE
file at all (which reads as an oversight rather than a deliberate choice, and gives no
pointer to what needs to happen next).
